  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe current methods rely on iterative optimization with binary/discrete structures and SLSQP, which may get stuck in local optima. The key idea is to use a structured optimization approach based on sparse grid representations combined with a physics-based interpretation. We model the function h(x) as a superposition of harmonic patterns and use gradient-based optimization with bound constraints. This leverages insights from wavelet theory and harmonic analysis to capture the periodic nature of overlap, leading to smoother and more structured solutions than step-function approaches. The planned approach includes multi-resolution optimization, gradient projection techniques, and a harmonic embedding to ensure the solution remains near the optimum.\n\nMathematical specification:\nWe represent h(x) on [0,2] using a piecewise constant refinement grid. The optimization variables are a multi-level index s_j, and a coefficient a_j for each segment. The function is built by:\n\n1.  Candidate function representation:\n    h(x) = \u2211_{j=1}^N a_j \\cdot \\text{rect}(x - x_j)\n\n2.  Overlap integral:\n    C_5 = \\max_{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}} \\left| \\int_0^2 h(x) [1 - h(x+k)]  dx \\right|\n\n3.  Constraints:\n    -  0 \u2264 a_j \u2264 1 for all j\n    -  \\sum_j a_j \\cdot l_j = 1, where l_j is the segment length (dx)\n\n4.  The objective is to minimize C_5.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1.  Parent handling and initialization:\n    - Input `initial_h_values` (n=250 is provided by the valuation)\n    - If initial_h_values exists, use it as base solution\n    - Compute grid resolution and feasibility projection\n    - Project to binary representation based on maxima\n\n2.  Core optimization:\n    - Use stochastic box adjustment in [0,1] with feasibility projection\n    - Apply gradient-based descent with line-search: for each candidate, compute:\n        \u2207(C_5) = \\sum_{k} \\left[ h(x) [1 - h(x+k)] \\right] * (derivatives of rect functions)\n    - Update parameters: \n        a_j = a_j - \u03b1 * \u2202/\u2202a_j\n        with projection: max(0, min(1, a_j))\n\n3.  Constraint handling:\n    - Use Moreau-Yosida relaxation for projection:\n        proj_h(a) = \\text{argmin}_a \\|a - \\hat{a}\\|^2_2 + \\frac{1}{\\epsilon} \\mathbf{1}_{\\sum a_j \\cdot l_j = 1}\n\n4.  Search choices:\n    - Representation: piecewise constant with variable segmentation\n    - Optimization: stochastic gradient descent with momentum (momentum factor = 0.9)\n    - Resolution progression: start from parent grid, refine in promising areas\n    - Use directional search based on boundary detection\n\n5.  Budget and robustness:\n    - Time budget: allocate gradient computation of 0.5s per call\n    - Monitor objective: stop if improvement < 1e-6 for 10 iterations\n    - Multiplicative restart: if loss plateaus, restart from neighborhood\n    - Progress: check objective every 500 iterations\n\n6.  Validation and return contract:\n    - Verify objectivity by re-evaluating using parent objective.py\n    - Ensure h(x) \u2208 [0,1] by projection/rounding\n    - Compare grid to parent grid by resampling and mode 'full' correlation\n    - Requirements: compute the exact overlap score, projection must satisfy \u2211 a_j * l_j = 1, and output parameters must be [0,1] for each a_j",
